% ============================================================================
% reference-line-hemisphere-location.query — a worked recall over the
% geography reference-line-hemisphere-location library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "which hemisphere is
% the Tropic of Cancer in?": it states no geography fact of its own — it
% only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `reference_line_hemisphere_location` rows
% and returns the hemisphere + the table's source/locator/trust. A line the
% cited span gives no single containing hemisphere for abstains honestly —
% the engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli reference-line-hemisphere-location.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "reference-line-hemisphere-location.adj"

? reference_line_hemisphere_location(tropic_of_cancer, $Hemisphere)  % expect northern
? reference_line_hemisphere_location($Line, southern)                % reverse bind — expect tropic_of_capricorn
? reference_line_hemisphere_location(equator, $Hemisphere)           % expect abstain — equator's own cited span states no single containing hemisphere (it DIVIDES hemispheres, already captured in reference_line_hemisphere_split)
